{"title":"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle has a radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b34d3cc8d92f18962c19e3ed3b93c265ea9db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10}{(a^2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"19\" /> and a circumference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b6b0e5c76430c7f97c07f631e6ad3bcb1c4ca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{10}{(b^4)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"19\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00ca1d0113fd12d4b87405c9483f5c5fcd8d8184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/f/d9f239540e69528094eb2885577ebfd6d602e436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{4\\pi} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{\\pi} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 2\\pi \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 10^{2\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"406\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumference of the circle, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the circle. \n</p><p>Using log properties, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/6/1469d2b32097eaa9edae11537c1edfb1b7cee1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=\\log_{10}{(b^4)}=4\\log_{10}{(b)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"206\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e69a95abc3206b377156285907990351e4f07f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\log_{10}{(a^2)}=2\\log_{10}{(a)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"203\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07ad7caf69ba14640d888bda20e93c71474794ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=2\\pi r$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60e2cb262251b46de26399796c51bf00920de879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\log_{10}{(b)}=2\\pi\\cdot2\\log_{10}{(a)} \\Rightarrow \\log_{a}{b} = \\frac{\\log_{10}{(b)}}{\\log_{10}{(a)}}=\\pi \\Rightarrow C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"449\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B\">2008 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=